|move6 = V  | 5,000
}}

===Unlocking Dough Raids===
# The player must have the {{Icon|God's Chalice|25}} and {{Conjured Cocoa|10}} [[Conjured Cocoa]]s.
#* It is recommended to grind [[Conjured Cocoa]]s while waiting for other things to spawn, such as [[Elite Pirates]] or [[God's Chalice]] from a [[chest]] in order to save time.
# The player must use the [[materials]] collected above to trade for the [[Sweet Chalice]] from the [[Sweet Crafter]] located at the [[Chocolate Land]] in the [[Sea of Treats]].
# The player must talk to [[drip_mama]] after 500 [[enemies]] have been defeated at [[Cake Land]] to summon [[Dough King]] using the [[Sweet Chalice]].
#* It is recommended to do this in a [[Private Servers|private server]] with a few friends, as trollers or exploiters could spawn the [[Cake Prince]] instead.
#* The player who has the [[Sweet Chalice]] should be the one checking [[drip_mama]] and opening the portal while other players kill [[enemies]], as the [[Sweet Chalice]] will be lost upon death or disconnection of the player owning it which would be devastating.
# Once defeated, the [[Dough King]] will drop the [[Red Key]] (assuming the player did 10% or more of the total damage to Dough King).
# The player can use the [[Red Key]] to permanently unlock the door inside the [[Cake Scientist|Cake Castle]] at the [[Cake Land]].
#* Even if the player disconnects or dies with the [[Red Key]], they will still be able to buy Dough [[Raids|Raid]] [[Microchip]]s unless they never obtained it.
Talk to the [[Cake Scientist]] to buy a Dough [[Raids|Raid]] [[Microchip]] at the cost of {{Fragment|1,000}} every 2 hours, or a physical [[Blox Fruit]] that is worth at least {{Money|1,000,000}}. Players will now be able to buy Dough [[Raids|Raid]] [[Microchip]]s from the [[Mysterious Scientist]] upon completing the previous steps.

