==Tips & Tricks==
* While in the [[Water|Sea]], using {{Ability|V}} or {{Ability|V|1}} on somebody will make them stop and take damage from the [[water]]. (Unless they are using [[Shark|Shark V2]] or above.)
* {{Ability|F}} can be used on the [[water]] if the player has the [[Shark]] [[Races|race]] upgraded to V2 or higher.
* Falling from a great height while using the {{Ability|F|1}} ability into the [[water]] can sometimes deactivate the ability, unless the user is using [[Shark#Version 1-3|Shark V2]] or above.
* {{Ability|F}} climbs slope much faster, but it cannot climb walls. (Not to be mistaken for {{Ability|F|1}}, which can climb walls, but climbs slopes slower).
* {{Ability|Z|1}} has a bigger explosion and will knock the player further back when held. Since being fully held only takes about a second, so unless used in a combo, it is better to hold it.
* If the user holds {{Ability|X|1}}'s ground variation, it becomes slightly taller and has a bigger overall look and hitbox. It does not deal more damage.
* It is recommended to use [[Angel]] V4's '''King's Rule''' [[gear]] while using {{Ability|C|1}}, since the opponent is damaged by the King's Rule aura at the start and the end, dealing more damage. Using [[Cyborg]]'s V3 ability, [[Energy Core]], can produce similar results. Using the {{Ability|V|1}} while having King's Rule aura can damage the enemy even more when the user brings them close enough.
* {{Ability|F|1}} and {{Ability|C|1}} abilities look similar, with the only differences being their size and speed, so it is recommended to keep distance. (Note: {{Ability|C|1}}'s donut at a long distance can be [[Instinct]] dodged or just damage the donut in any way without being hit. [Using a long-range attack or [[gun]] is recommended.])
* [[Human#Version 4|Human]] V4's '''Psycho''' Tier 2 ability allows the player to hold down moves without their moves being interrupted/canceled when damaged. This is really useful as some of Dough's moves are easily cancelable by other moves and this allows the player to hold down an ability like the {{Ability|V|1}} without getting interrupted.
* As Dough itself is weak in air, a [[fighting styles|fighting style]] that has good mobility/combo starter in air, like [[Godhuman]], is recommended.
* Using [[Spikey Trident]] or [[Cursed Dual Katana]] is very good to pair with Dough because they both have good mobility moves and moves that can grab an enemy (such as  [[Spikey Trident]] z or [[Cursed Dual Katana]] X). This is useful during {{Ability|C|1}}.
* A good alternative is [[Sanguine Art]] or [[Yama]], since both of them are very strong in the air, and [[Yama]] can give the user insane movement when pairing with the [[Skull Guitar]] dash tech and also providing a very solid stun/combo starter ([[Yama]] x). Be aware that the user needs to be close to the opponent to deal damage due to most of [[Sanguine Art]] and [[Yama]]'s move are close-ranged.

==Trivia==
* Dough is the priciest fruit awakening, alongside [[Phoenix]] with them both being [[Raids#Raid Types|Advanced fruit awakenings]].
* All of the awakened abilities are affected by [[Skins|Aura Colors]], changing the outline in all the moves and "electricity" effects (the only other fruits in which the moves are affected by the Aura Color being [[Rubber]] and [[Spider]]).
* Dough is the only fruit in the entire game where its attacks are buffed by [[Aura]], specifically its '''[TAP] Normal Attack''' and {{Ability|Z|1}} when awakened.
** Additionally, depending on whether the user has [[Aura]] activated or not, the sound effects of Dough's '''[TAP] Normal Attack''' and {{Ability|V|1}} will be different.
* When the user uses {{Ability|Z|1}} or {{Ability|X|1}} (Air variant), they can see that their arm disappears but rebuilds itself with mass.
* Dough's unawakened {{Ability|C}} and {{Ability|C|1}} abilities bear a visual resemblance to an ability from an old game made by [[Mygame43 (Player)|mygame43]], [https://www.roblox.com/games/566399244/SOLAR-Elemental-Battlegrounds Elemental Battlegrounds].
* If the user uses {{Ability|C|1}} while not using any [[Skins|Aura Colors]], the effects will be red by default.
* Dough’s {{Ability|C|1}} (awakened/unawakened) can be used as an alternative for its '''[F] Scorching Donut move (awakened/unawakened), but only for up to four seconds.'''
* {{Ability|V|1}} will appear with bigger hands when used with [[aura]], while without it will appear significantly skinnier.
* Dough is the only [[Mythical]] fruit that can be awakened.
* Dough is the first {{Mythical}} [[Elemental]] fruit, while the second is [[Gas]].
** Dough used to be a [[Natural]] fruit that had the Elemental Reflex passive only if the user's [[Instinct]] was turned on, but this was later changed, and Dough was made entirely [[Elemental]].
* Awakened Dough's {{Ability|Z|1}} ability projectile is actually a small [[aura]]-covered fist after being fired.
* Repeatedly using '''[TAP] Normal Attack''' and/or aiming {{Ability|V|1}} in the same spot will leave a crack on the ground, which increases in size the more the user punches in that spot. When using {{Ability|V|1}}, the crack will briefly appear "scorched".
* When using '''[X] Pastry River''' (Air variant), the opponent gets trapped inside a ball made out of dough that explodes when the fist pushes it towards the ground, ending the move.

